/-!
# Checked enumeration of the marked M₂₄ subgroup

Positive words in the four certified Witt-design permutations give 1024
permutations. Their images of points 0, 1, and 5 have strictly increasing
base-24 encodings, so the permutations are distinct. A transition table
records left multiplication by each generator on all 24 points.

For efficient kernel checking, the tables use binary lookup. Point images
are evaluated directly from the words using the certified generator actions.
The data are generated by `source/generate.py`, which is untrusted: all
identities are checked below.

This is the finite calculation for the subgroup-order input to the Sylow
normalizer argument (Aschbacher–Smith, printed p.511; GLS3, Table 5.3e).
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.M24LocalGeometry.SylowNormalizer.OrderEnumeration

set_option maxRecDepth 100000

/-- Binary tables keep the kernel's lookup depth logarithmic. -/
@[reducible] def Table (α : Type) : ℕ → Type
  | 0 => α
  | n + 1 => Table α n × Table α n

def lookup {α : Type} : (n : ℕ) → Table α n → ℕ → α
  | 0, t, _ => t
  | n + 1, t, i => lookup n (if i % 2 = 0 then t.1 else t.2) (i / 2)

